# The reference wakes a snoozed thread early when a message lands after the
# snooze was set -- but only where the caller holds the row's clocks: the
# sidebar row menu. The tab menu has no row and stays due-only. Both seeds
# are one thread, t6: snoozed until 13:00Z at 11:59Z (runner clock 12:00Z),
# a message at 11:59:30Z, so the row menu reads Snooze again while the tab
# menu still reads "Snoozed until 1:00 PM". t7 is snoozed with no message
# after it and reads "Snoozed until 1:00 PM" in both. Assertions do not block
# the next command and retry for MAX_FRAMES=30, so each menu is held open for
# 32 frames before the Escape that would close it.
# settings: {"window_width":1100,"window_height":760,"open_tabs":["t6"],"active_tab":"t6","theme":"dark"}
# env: HANABI_MOCK_SNOOZES=t6:1781528400:1781524740,t7:1781528400:1781524740 HANABI_MOCK_ROW_CLOCKS=t6:1781524770000
require_thread t6
require_thread t7
wait_frames 20
expect_text "SKU backfill — my name for it"
expect_text "coordinating 3 shard workers"
right_click_ui chat_row_id_t6
wait_frames 8
expect_text "Snooze"
expect_no_text "Snoozed until"
wait_frames 32
key ESCAPE
wait_frames 4
right_click_ui chat_row_id_t7
wait_frames 8
expect_text "Snoozed until 1:00 PM"
wait_frames 32
key ESCAPE
wait_frames 4
right_click_ui tab_t6
wait_frames 8
expect_text "Snoozed until 1:00 PM"
wait_frames 32
key ESCAPE
